# Prepares the built fixture orc-bard-reapply-seed1 for the checks that load it (bd inc-10v7f).
# The old fixture, a .sav, held this state: wizard mode on with Auto-Identify Items and Free Advancement; the
# Orc Bard raised from level 1 to Bard 6 (five G presses; each takes the first attribute bonus, the first feat
# and the spell list as offered); every monster gone, so nothing walks up and changes hit points.
# Ruling V7-1: a fixture holds only the created character, so the checks that need the state make it here.
@while "more --" SPACE
w
@while "Enter wizard mode" y
@until "Wizard Mode Options" w
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN SPACE              # Auto-Identify Items
DOWN SPACE              # Free Advancement
ESC

d
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "You feel stronger" SPACE
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Learn Spells: Level" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "You feel stronger" SPACE
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Learn Spells: Level" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "You feel stronger" SPACE
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Learn Spells: Level" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "You feel stronger" SPACE
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Learn Spells: Level" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "You feel stronger" SPACE
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Learn Spells: Level" ESC
@expect "Class  Bard 6 "
ESC

w
@choose "Genocide Everything"   # nothing may walk up and change HP
@until "HP:" ESC
